  "prompt": "You are a credit analyst at a major commercial bank's Technology & Industrials coverage group. The bank's Risk Committee has flagged Tesla, Inc. (TSLA) for a quarterly credit review following the release of its Q1 2026 10-Q filing. The committee wants a concise credit memo assessing Tesla's current financial health, recent performance trends, and key credit risk factors to determine whether to maintain, adjust, or recommend changes to the company's revolving credit facility.\n\nMaterials Provided:\n- The attached financial data package for Tesla, Inc. (TSLA), containing quarterly and annual financial metrics from XBRL filings, including revenue, profitability, balance sheet data, and operating metrics for FY2025 and Q1 2026.\n\nTask Requirements:\n1. Prepare a Credit Memo for Tesla, Inc. with the following sections:\n   - Executive Summary: A one-paragraph overview of Tesla's credit profile, including overall assessment and recommendation (maintain, upgrade, or downgrade).\n   - Company Overview: Brief description of Tesla's business and sector.\n   - Recent Financial Performance: Analyze revenue and profitability trends using Q1 2026 data compared to FY2025 quarterly run-rate. Calculate and discuss gross margin, operating margin, and net margin for Q1 2026.\n   - Balance Sheet Analysis: Evaluate liquidity (cash position), leverage (debt-to-equity ratio using total liabilities and stockholders' equity), and asset growth. Use Q1 2026 balance sheet data.\n   - Key Credit Strengths and Risks: Identify at least two strengths and two risks from the financial data provided.\n   - Conclusion and Recommendation: Reiterate the credit assessment with supporting rationale.\n\n2. Constraints:\n   - Focus exclusively on data from the provided financial package (FY2025 and Q1 2026).\n   - Calculate all margin percentages to one decimal place.\n   - Use the company's full legal name (Tesla, Inc.) and ticker (TSLA) in the memo header.\n   - The memo should be professional, concise, and suitable for presentation to the bank's Risk Committee.\n\nDeliverable Specification:\n   - Output as a PDF document titled 'Credit Memo - Tesla, Inc.'.\n   - Include a memorandum-style header with To, From, Date, and Re lines.\n   - The document should be 2-3 pages, with clear section headings as listed above.",
